{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790007385764,"sessionID":"ses_f3b3f396fffeYN20OUUXOIvstd","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_05_LVVEBLq3fvINmAxzk45N5691","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/proj/assert-berzelius/users/x_frrey/yul/benchmark/runs-opencode-deepseek-pilot/pypi-top-01-requests/hook/run-2/README.md","content":"# rest-fetcher\n\nA small Python project that fetches data from a REST API over HTTP using\n[`requests`](https://requests.readthedocs.io/).\n\n## Setup\n\n```bash\nuv venv\nuv pip install -e \".[dev]\"\n```\n\nOr with plain pip:\n\n```bash\npython -m venv .venv\n. .venv/bin/activate\npip install -e \".[dev]\"\n```\n\n## Usage\n\nCommand line:\n\n```bash\nrest-fetcher https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests \\\n  -H \"Accept=application/vnd.github+json\" \\\n  -p per_page=5\n```\n\nAs a library:\n\n```python\nfrom rest_fetcher import fetch_json\n\ndata = fetch_json(\"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests\")\nprint(data[\"full_name\"])\n```\n\n## Tests\n\n```bash\npytest\n```\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/proj/assert-berzelius/users/x_frrey/yul/benchmark/runs-opencode-deepseek-pilot/pypi-top-01-requests/hook/run-2/README.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1790007385620,"end":1790007385755}},"id":"prt_0c4c11947001oiHJ53GNER5bRN","sessionID":"ses_f3b3f396fffeYN20OUUXOIvstd","messageID":"msg_0c4c0fed1001t9LAdshayHcKGn"}}
